WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.600
Have you ever wondered
if there’s a natural way

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.160
to lower your high blood pressure,
guard against Alzheimer's,

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.440
lose weight, and feel better?
Well, it turns out there is!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.680
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.520
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.120
Today we discover how
eating a plant-based diet

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.560
offers less exposure to
the industrial pollutants

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:26.560
that bioaccumulate
up the food chain.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.840
We lack robust safety data

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.320
on most of the estimated
30,000 chemicals

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.560
in wide commercial use

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:36.600
registered under the U.S.
Toxic Substances Control Act.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.240
But the greatest concern may lie

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.640
in the long-banned
legacy chemicals

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.160
that continue to contaminate
the food supply

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:47.640
known as PLOPs-persistent
lipophilic organic pollutants.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:52.800
These include dioxins, PCBs,
and insecticides such as DDT.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.280
How do we drop the PLOPs?

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:57.680
Today, most DDT
comes from meat,

00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.040
particularly fish.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.760
The oceans are essentially
humanity's sewer;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.160
everything eventually flows
into the sea.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:08.320
Hexachlorobenzene is
another banned pesticide

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:09.720
that may be carcinogenic,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.560
but is more evenly spread
among animal food sources,

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:16.240
whereas PCBs are
also mostly a fish thing.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.080
PCBs are a different set
of banned chemicals,

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.040
once widely used
as insulating fluid

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.720
in electrical equipment.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.320
A study of more than 12,000
food and feed samples

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.920
across 18 countries

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.920
found that the highest
PCB contamination

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.000
was found in fish and fish oil,

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:33.760
followed by eggs, then dairy,
then other meats.

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.320
Salmon may have
the highest concentration

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:37.480
(with farmed-raised salmon

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:39.560
having consistently higher
contaminant levels

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.880
than wild-caught)
followed by canned tuna.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:45.480
But since people don't tend
to eat a lot of fish,

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.280
other meat may be the largest
exposure for most people.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.160
The lowest contamination
was found

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.720
at the bottom
of the food chain in plants,

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.560
which can average 7 to 20 times
fewer overall PCB

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:58.760
and dioxin-like chemicals

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:02.760
compared to ocean
or freshwater fish.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.280
That's one of the advantages

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.800
to eating more plant-based
in the modern world.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:09.160
By eating from the lowest rung
of the food chain,

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.640
we suffer less exposure
to the industrial pollutants

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.720
that bioaccumulate
up the ladder.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.400
Every year
in the United States,

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:17.280
billions of pounds

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:19.600
of slaughterhouse by-products
are produced,

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.640
the vast majority of which

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.080
are fed right back
to the farm animals,

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.400
particularly chickens,

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.560
which can recycle
toxic heavy metals

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.960
and industrial chemicals
back into the food supply.

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:31.280
Lead builds up in bones

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.760
and mercury attaches
to the protein

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.080
(which is why egg whites can
have four times more mercury

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.000
than do yolks).

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.440
Most of the lead
in the bone meal

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:42.640
passes right through
the animals into their waste,

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.520
but then producers
can take that waste-

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:45.880
cow, pig, and chicken feces-

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.160
and feed it
back to the animals again.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.160
So, you can see
how the levels of contaminants

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.720
might build up in their bodies

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.280
even when the animals themselves

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:55.640
may be natural herbivores.

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.560
Lower pollutant levels
may help explain

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.440
why those eating plant-based

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:01.440
appear to be less likely
to develop

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.800
all forms of cancer combined,

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.200
but their role in longevity
is unknown.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.600
Heavy metals such as lead

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.120
appear to accelerate
human aging,

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.080
and most population studies
have suggested

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.240
a strong association
between exposure

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.200
to higher levels
of environmental pollutants

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:18.920
and shorter telomeres.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.400
However, only a few
have been found

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.920
to be significantly related
to premature death.

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:25.440
One such contaminant

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.840
is the long-banned pesticide
beta-hexachlorocyclohexane.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:30.840
Higher levels in the blood

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.840
correlate with higher
all-cause mortality.

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:36.720
A study of the breast milk
from two sisters

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:38.040
with different dietary habits

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:41.360
offered a clue
on a way to lower exposure.

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.120
The levels
of beta-hexachlorocyclohexane,

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.800
as well as PCBs, DDT,

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.040
and another banned pesticide
dieldrin

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.080
were much lower
in the breast milk

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.600
from the vegetarian mother
than the milk of her sister,

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.200
who was also breastfeeding
at the time,

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.040
but included meat in her diet.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:01.040
Studies of the pollutants
in breast milk of vegetarians

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:02.760
dating back over 30 years

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.760
have found the average levels
of some pollutants

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:08.320
were 50 to 100 times lower
in the vegetarians

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.480
compared
to the national average.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.600
In fact, for the six
out of seven pollutants

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.400
they looked at,
there wasn't even an overlap

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.880
in the range of scores;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.520
the highest vegetarian value
was lower

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.800
than the lowest value obtained
in the general population.

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.600
Chlorinated PCBs
have also been associated

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.880
with increased mortality risk,

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.400
suggesting we should
minimize exposure,

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:34.600
which basically means
a reduction in animal fats.

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.960
The blood of those eating
strictly plant-based diets

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.120
were found to be
"significantly less polluted"

00:04:40.120 --> 00:04:42.000
regarding a whole series
of PCBs,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.520
including those found
in the study

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:46.120
to be associated
with increased mortality,

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:49.000
but their lower levels
of beta-hexachlorocyclohexane

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.800
did not reach
statistical significance.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.800
Those eating plant-based diets
have also been found

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:56.800
to have markedly lower levels
of dioxins in their bodies,

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.560
as well as decreased
contamination

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.360
with flame-retardant
chemical pollutants

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.400
known as PBDEs.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.400
No surprise given the sources
of flame retardant chemicals

00:05:05.400 --> 00:05:07.040
in the food supply.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.920
Again, even though
the highest levels

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:10.800
of flame retardants
in the U.S. food supply

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:12.320
have been found in fish,

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:15.800
the primary source of intake
for most Americans is poultry,

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:17.280
just because we eat
so much chicken,

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.520
followed by processed meat.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.240
For some reason, U.S. chickens

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.720
are about 10 to 20 times
more contaminated

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:26.960
than chickens tested
from some other countries.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.200
The longer people
go without meat,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.160
the lower their levels
appear to fall.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.720
Eating healthier
can also reduce

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.600
the concentrations
of heavy metals in your body.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:38.480
The levels of mercury
in the hair

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.040
of those eating
more plant-based diets

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:41.840
were found to be
up to ten times lower

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.720
than of those who ate fish,

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:46.400
but you don't know
if it's cause and effect

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:49.480
until you put it to the test.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:50.720
Within three months
of switching

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:53.640
to a plant-based diet,
the levels of mercury, lead,

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.120
and cadmium
growing out in your hair

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:58.800
appear to drop significantly

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.360
(but build back up
when meat and eggs

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.600
are added back into the diet).

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.160
Unlike heavy metals, though,

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:09.120
some organochlorine pollutants
can stick around for decades.

00:06:09.120 --> 00:06:11.280
A USDA examination
of the levels

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:13.920
of dioxin-like compounds
in U.S. meat and poultry

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:17.720
indicated a possible concern
for U.S. public health,

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:19.880
but really mostly for children.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.680
The typical U.S. adult
daily exposure in meat

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.640
was well below the EPA
established safety limit.

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:27.800
Only children
chronically consuming

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.500
the average daily servings
of meat or poultry

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:32.080
with the highest levels
might exceed it.

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:34.440
Taking all 33
chemical pollutants in meat

00:06:34.440 --> 00:06:37.560
shown to be potentially
carcinogenic into account,

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:39.160
some European toxicologists

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.080
suggest limiting
children's consumption

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.880
of beef, pork, and chicken

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:46.160
to a combined total of no more
than five servings a month,

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:48.280
so an average of no more than
like one serving of meat

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:49.840
every six days or so.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.920
In Europe,
lamb is the most contaminated,

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:54.760
and the recommendation
calls for adults

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:56.320
to eat no more than
a single serving

00:06:56.320 --> 00:06:58.440
every four or five months.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:06:59.200
Surprisingly, as I explored
in a previous video,

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.040
the consumption of organic meat

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.720
does not seem to diminish
the cancer-causing potential

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:05.640
associated with the PLOPs
in meat.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:07.760
All samples were found
to be contaminated

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.120
with minimal differences

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.480
between meat raised organic
versus conventional.

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.440
What can we do
to reduce exposure?

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.120
Eat high-fiber foods,

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:18.360
as fiber can bind
to some of the contaminants

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:20.800
and flush them out of the body.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:23.400
Exercise, as blood levels
of persistent pollutants

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.560
have been found to be lower

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:26.880
among physically active
individuals,

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.000
perhaps due to sweating,

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.320
or due to a potential boost
in detoxing enzymes,

00:07:31.320 --> 00:07:33.320
or increased clearance
through the bile,

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.320
at least in rats.

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.600
Given current
contamination levels,

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.400
"meat consumption in general...

00:07:39.400 --> 00:07:42.160
should be
significantly modified downward,

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:44.880
as much
and as soon as possible,"

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:47.880
though until then,
consumers can reduce exposures

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.640
to dioxins and dioxin-like
compounds like PCBs

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.800
by trimming fat
when preparing meat,

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:53.600
and further trim

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:56.640
and thoroughly drain fat
after cooking.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:59.040
The Best Dietary Detox

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:04.160
is to not tox
in the first place.

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:04.840
Finally today,

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:08.760
we look at how we might help flush
the pollutants stored in our fat

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:12.920
that come spilling out into our
bloodstream during weight loss.

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:16.840
Most persistent industrial pollutants,
like organochlorine pesticides

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:20.960
such as DDT and PCBs,
were banned several decades ago,

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.280
and dioxin emission
is strictly regulated.

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:27.800
However, we’re still exposed to these
chemicals through several routes,

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:31.120
the major source of which
is contaminated food,

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:35.800
especially fatty animal products
such as fish, meat, and milk.

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:38.640
When we eat these chemicals,
they get primarily stored

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.440
in our own fatty tissue
where they slowly leach out

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.560
into our bloodstream,
but better in our fat

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:47.000
than in our brain
or other vital organs.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.000
Having more body fat may
actually play a protective role

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:52.720
by sequestering
the toxins away,

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:57.960
but they can come spilling
out when we lose weight.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:00.320
Body weight loss increases
the concentrations

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.960
of potentially toxic pollutants
in obese individuals.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.680
Of the 19 pollutants studied,
they all went up,

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:09.080
15 significantly so.

00:09:09.080 --> 00:09:12.360
Every study that has looked at it
found increased blood levels

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.880
of toxic pollutants
accompanying weight loss

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.760
whether induced by diet
or bariatric surgery:

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:24.560
increases between 14 and 388
percent with a large enough loss.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.120
The more weight that’s lost,
the higher the pollutant levels

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.160
climb because all those
chemicals stored in your fat

00:09:29.160 --> 00:09:32.200
over all those years
come spilling out.

00:09:32.200 --> 00:09:34.840
The theoretical concern is that
if released into the blood

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.920
at a faster rate
than they are cleared,

00:09:36.920 --> 00:09:39.360
the levels of these compounds
could become toxic,

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.000
causing side effects, such
as sweating, headache, and nausea,

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:48.560
but the opposite happened when
PCB-poisoned patients were fasted.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.400
In 1979, about 2000 people
in Taiwan were exposed

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.600
via an industrial accident
that contaminated rice oil,

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:58.560
leading them to have a
higher body toxicity burden

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.360
than even long-time
consumers of seafood.

00:10:01.360 --> 00:10:03.240
But after a modified
fasting regimen,

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:06.320
all 16 patients they tried
it on showed improvements,

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:09.920
with some enjoying dramatic
relief of their sufferings,

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:11.880
but this was after just
a few days of fasting;

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:14.960
so, they couldn’t have really
lost that much body fat.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:18.000
And, they didn’t measure
PCBs before and after;

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:21.560
so, it’s not clear they were
experiencing some sort of detox,

00:10:21.560 --> 00:10:23.520
nor what relevance
this has for people

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:26.360
who haven’t been
acutely poisoned.

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:28.640
The initial rise in pollutant
levels in the first year

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:31.780
of weight loss may
eventually stabilize or fall.

00:10:31.780 --> 00:10:34.440
Check out what
happened in Biosphere 2,

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:38.360
a remarkable experiment designed
to be a completely closed ecosystem,

00:10:38.360 --> 00:10:40.520
the longest sustained
period of humans isolated

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:43.560
in a confined environment
on record.

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:45.080
But due to crop failures,
it turned

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.120
into a 2-year experiment
of calorie restriction.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:50.520
They all lost about 25 pounds
in the first 6 months

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.880
and stabilized there,
and while the levels of PCBs

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:57.880
and a DDT metabolite
known as DDE initially went up,

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.320
they appeared to start
coming back down,

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:03.360
but that initial spike
is quite a jump.

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.840
That’s one of the reasons
health authorities recommend women

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:08.800
don’t try to slim down
during breast-feeding.

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:13.840
Breast is still best regardless,
but you can keep your levels lower

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.640
by not going out of
your way to lose weight

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.280
until after breastfeeding
is finished.

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.640
What can one do to help flush
the contaminants during weight loss?

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:25.280
One of the reasons the pollutant
levels in the biosphere subjects

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:28.760
eventually dropped is because
they were eating a high fiber diet

00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:33.040
centered around fruits, whole grains,
beans, nuts, and vegetables,

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.920
and we know that fiber can
bind to these pollutants

00:11:35.920 --> 00:11:38.640
and potentially flush
them out of the body.

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.240
So, when losing weight,
eating lots of whole grains

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:45.120
may be important to increase
the elimination of pollutants

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.680
while, of course, cutting down
on animal fat, including fish,

00:11:47.680 --> 00:11:52.080
so you don’t pile on
extra at the same time.

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:55.880
What about just
eating some Pringles?

00:11:55.880 --> 00:11:58.480
What was the dietary intervention
in this randomized trial

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:00.960
to decrease the body
burden of pollutants?

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:04.240
Subjects were randomized
to 24 fat-free Pringles

00:12:04.240 --> 00:12:09.480
a day or regular Pringles.
What?! Why?

00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:12.840
It all started with this
crazy case report of a guy

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.800
heavily contaminated by PCBs
who managed to rid himself

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:19.680
of 90 percent by losing
weight eating potato chips

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:23.520
made out of the fake fat olestra,
which doesn’t get absorbed,

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.320
and so appears to pull
pollutants out of the bloodstream

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:29.400
into the stool for elimination.

00:12:29.400 --> 00:12:33.600
It works in mice, increasing the
excretion of hexachlorobenzene

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.840
30-fold and cutting the levels
in their brains in half,

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:42.000
but in people, the drop in PCB blood
levels with the olestra Pringles

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:46.360
was not statistically significantly
greater, and for some reason,

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:51.000
LDL bad cholesterol levels shot
up 28 points in the olestra group.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:54.280
And, while olestra and drugs
like cholestyramine may absorb

00:12:54.280 --> 00:12:56.840
pollutants and remove
them from your system,

00:12:56.840 --> 00:13:00.040
they also may cause you
to dump fat-soluble vitamins.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.840
So, to get the best
of both worlds,

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.840
losing pollution
without losing vitamins,

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:10.160
fiber-rich foods
maybe our best choice.

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.240
Instead of olestra
supplementation to detox,

00:13:13.240 --> 00:13:19.040
why not try to not tox
so much in the first place.

